// Committed mesh-integrity baselines, read by `level_check`.
//
// The check is relative: an error only when the count rises meaningfully above
// the figure recorded here. Re-commit these numbers when terrain generation or
// meshing changes on purpose. The count is per level *file*, not per segment
// definition: a segment instanced twice contributes twice.
//
// All three levels read **zero** open edges as of the heightfield-degeneracy
// fix. Every figure recorded before it — 218, 22 and 1174 — came from lattice
// samples landing exactly on an iso-surface, which turns out to be one bug and
// not the three separate ones they were attributed to. The cave counts were not
// cave noise finding an ambiguous marching-cubes case; they were
// `carve_with_sdf` encoding a density of exactly zero wherever the noise
// equalled its threshold. The test_segments figure was not the deck-meets-
// terrain union either: a deck is authored at a round height, so its own
// encoded surface sat on the lattice. Debiasing both density writes closed all
// of them.
//
// Zero is now the expectation rather than a tolerance. `level_check` still
// permits a small absolute rise before it errors, so a rise recorded here is a
// real regression — read it as one.
//
// `subsidence` is the exception, and its 26 is recorded as a **known defect,
// not an accepted tolerance**. Bisected by segment and then by feature:
//
//     plain heightfield, 0.5 m voxels, 64 x 64      4
//       + Tunnel                                   +0
//       + Caves                                   +10
//       + Shaft                                    -1
//       + Island                                   +9
//     pit_rim (1 m voxels, Plateaus/Ramp/Pillar)    4
//     spoil_block                                   0
//
// The floor of 4 comes from a bare noisy heightfield with no volumes at all, so
// the residual is scale-dependent rather than feature-specific — the three test
// levels read zero because they are smaller, not because the class is closed.
// Nudging every authored surface off the voxel lattice changed nothing (26 →
// 27), so this is not the lattice-coincidence bug above. Do not treat this
// entry as permission to add more; drive it to zero and delete it.
(
    entries: [
        (level: "test_arena.level.ron", triangles: 193828, open_edges: 0),
        (level: "test_empty_terrain.level.ron", triangles: 100276, open_edges: 0),
        (level: "test_segments.level.ron", triangles: 224756, open_edges: 0),
        (level: "subsidence.level.ron", triangles: 301284, open_edges: 26),
    ],
)
